# Desirables, Chapter 7: Deformation theory à la Schlessinger

The source section (`books/desirables.tex:110-128`) is an editorial roadmap.
It points to the chapters on formal deformation theory, examples of
deformation problems, deformation theory, and the full cotangent complex.  It
also lists deformations of rings and modules, ringed spaces and sheaves, and
ringed topoi and sheaves as topics, and says that the naive cotangent complex
is used there for obstructions, first-order deformations, and infinitesimal
automorphisms.  It finally notes that this material has applications to the
algebraicity of moduli stacks in later chapters.

Those cross-references and topic descriptions do not give a mathematical
signature for a new definition or theorem.  In particular, the section does
not state a deformation functor, a category of Artinian rings, a cotangent
complex, an obstruction map, or an assertion about any of them.  The
corresponding interfaces belong to the referenced chapters (and are already
formalized there where applicable), so this section contributes no standalone
Lean declaration.
